{"data": [{"id": "2122126586363498902", "author_id": "745712286359257088", "text": "@GithubProjects @libracoder you got featured 😄😄", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:36:20.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/noelzappy/status/2122126586363498902", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122118592619823306", "author_id": "1286119988743544832", "text": "@GithubProjects Wonder how this compares to Orbstack? Been using that as my daily driver for containers on Mac for a few months now.", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:04:34.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/gregcodesstuff/status/2122118592619823306", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 106, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122116850033234359", "author_id": "560037158", "text": "@francisvgarcia @marthaelax @GithubProjects I agree with that. A lot of people prefer to create their own versions quickly and share them through interactions on X. Before, that wasn't very easy to do because of the complexity involved in making those decisions before AI came along. The problem is that people misuse AI", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:57:38.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/astranua/status/2122116850033234359", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122115222802432183", "author_id": "1642175512062697472", "text": "@GithubProjects It was made 2 weeks ago so prob not finna switch but very cool to see something like this but I feel like docker is just so industry standard now.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:51:10.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/hitvdrs_rblx/status/2122115222802432183", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 254, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122110339919863939", "author_id": "2104267291152011265", "text": "@astranua @GithubProjects If it works", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:31:46.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/Major5965/status/2122110339919863939", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122088396449333535", "author_id": "1720665183188922368", "text": "@VoidMai99193888 @GithubProjects Oui, pour du dev local ça vaut clairement le test. Gratuit, en beta, ultra léger (~10-15 Mo de daemon, VM qui dort après 60 s) et nettement plus rapide que Docker Desktop sur les benches (démarrage ~15-22 ms vs 180-240 ms). Tes commandes docker/Compose/buildx marchent", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:04:34.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2122088396449333535", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122088237489373371", "author_id": "1309883153880936450", "text": "@GithubProjects @grok ça vaut le coût ?", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:03:56.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/VoidMai99193888/status/2122088237489373371", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 98, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122087528090239461", "author_id": "1366194671504875521", "text": "@GithubProjects 速度差も気になりますが、docker CLI・Compose・buildxをそのまま使える点が移行判断では大きいですね。起動が速くても既存の開発フローを組み替えるなら、そこで得を使い切ってしまうので。", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:01:07.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/Rachel_hkz/status/2122087528090239461", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 158, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122077672608088368", "author_id": "75247361", "text": "@GithubProjects I’m looking at the docs and wondering why such a significant thing has a tagline of “and why it’s cool”\n\nTo me that doesn’t speak to the magnitude of the tool particularly well.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:21:58.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/davehewy/status/2122077672608088368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 639, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122070650084790464", "author_id": "1911871128412315648", "text": "@marthaelax @astranua @GithubProjects The problem is that these refactors are done outside of the original project and comunity does not maintain them. Developers are burning tokens for free, (and as every Rust refactor) is forgoten next week.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T20:54:03.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/francisvgarcia/status/2122070650084790464", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122063348615528735", "author_id": "1175878265246031875", "text": "@GithubProjects @godsend_joseph", "created_at": "2026-11-15T20:25:02.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/obiabo_immanuel/status/2122063348615528735", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122063308501270766", "author_id": "1175878265246031875", "text": "@GithubProjects Yo @libracoder", "created_at": "2026-11-15T20:24:53.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/obiabo_immanuel/status/2122063308501270766", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 396, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122060278044954972", "author_id": "2108999927762227200", "text": "@marthaelax @GithubProjects No im too lazy for that,", "created_at": "2026-11-15T20:12:50.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/mcanadolu/status/2122060278044954972", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122058043491803619", "author_id": "2114205000406605824", "text": "@UnexpectedOrder @GithubProjects 😂😂", "create